104w|a|Infolded; entangled; complicated; involved. ; Tacitly comprised; fairly to be understood, though not expressed in words; implied; as, an implicit contract or agreement. ; Resting on another; trusting in the word or authority of another, without doubt or reserve; unquestioning; complete; as, implicit confidence; implicit obedience.	j:tov,94,4~tov,94,4
