1063|v|To bring in from abroad; to introduce from without; especially, to bring (wares or merchandise) into a place or country from a foreign country, in the transactions of commerce; -- opposed to export. We import teas from China, coffee from Brasil, etc. ; To carry or include, as meaning or intention; to imply; to signify. ; To be of importance or consequence to; to have a bearing on; to concern. ; To signify; to purport; to be of moment.	d:21r7,17,3~21r7,17,3
